CORE
main.py
--unwind 5
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[.*exception\.[0-9]+\] .* line 5 uncaught exception: FAILURE$
^\[.*assertion\.1\] .* line 13 Python assertion: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
PLR 8.4: an exception no handler can catch ends the program. It is reported
where it is raised and the path ends there, instead of setting the exception
flag, which made every later statement conditional on it.
